problems.solution:
Invert around <imath>A</imath> with radius <imath>r,</imath> and let <imath>P'</imath> denote the image of <imath>P</imath> after inversion for all points <imath>P.</imath> Then, by the properties of inversion, <imath>\measuredangle{ADB}=\measuredangle{D'B'A}</imath> and <imath>\measuredangle{ACB}=\measuredangle{C'B'A},</imath> so <cmath>\measuredangle{ADB}+\measuredangle{BCA}=\measuredangle{D'B'A}+\measuredangle{AB'C'}=\measuredangle{C'B'D'}=90^\circ.</cmath>
Also, by the Inversion Distance Formula, <cmath>AC=\frac{r^2}{AC'},</cmath> <cmath>BD=\frac{r^2}{AD'\cdot AB'}\cdot B'D',</cmath> <cmath>AD=\frac{r^2}{AD'},</cmath> and <cmath>BC=\frac{r^2}{AB'\cdot AC'}\cdot B'C'.</cmath> Thus, we obtain 

\begin{align*}
AC\cdot BD&=AD\cdot BC\\
\frac{r^2}{AC'}\cdot\left(\frac{r^2}{AD'\cdot AB'}\cdot B'D'\right)&=\frac{r^2}{AD'}\cdot\left(\frac{r^2}{AB'\cdot AC'}\cdot B'C'\right)\\
B'D'&=B'C'.\\
\end{align*}

Hence, combining <imath>B'D'=B'C'</imath> and <imath>\measuredangle{C'B'D'}=90^\circ,</imath> we obtain <cmath>\frac{C'D'}{B'D'}=\sqrt{2}.</cmath> But 
\begin{align*}
\frac{C'D'}{B'D'}&=\frac{\frac{r^2}{AB'}\cdot\frac{r^2}{AC'\cdot AD'}\cdot C'D'}{\frac{r^2}{AC'}\cdot\frac{r^2}{AB'\cdot AD'}\cdot B'D'}\\
&=\frac{AB\cdot CD}{AC\cdot BD}
\end{align*}

by the Inversion distance formula. Thus, the desired ratio is <imath>\boxed{\sqrt{2}.}</imath>

